<!DOCTYPE alphabet SYSTEM "../alphabet.dtd">
<!-- Emoji alphabet (issue Dasher-Android #61, option 2).

     Language-neutral: any user can switch here from the toolbar to pick
     emoji, then switch back — the engine's alphabet switch API makes this
     a pure data asset. Nodes carry multi-codepoint labels (ZWJ sequences,
     variation selectors); AlphIO stores the full label string as the
     node's Text, so a selection commits the entire sequence atomically
     (see ReadCharAttributes: Text = "text" attr, default Display/label).

     Groups are kept to 9 topical clusters plus separators: Dasher's
     zooming interface needs a shallow tree — two zoom levels to any
     emoji. A flat 200-node root would be unusable.

     Frequencies: training_emoji.txt provides mild ordering priors
     (common juxtapositions); without training the engine falls back to
     symbol-order defaults (NodeCreationManager "Dasher will still work").
     NOTE: the trainer matches ONE code point per symbol lookup, so only
     single-codepoint emoji are learnable from the corpus. The 31
     multi-codepoint nodes (ZWJ sequences, VS16 variants like ✈️) always
     take default frequencies — a longest-match trainer would be needed
     to train those (engine follow-up, not blocking).
-->
